As mentioned earlier, a key ingredient in combination of congruence a lgorithms is the detection and
factorisation of y-smooth numbers. The main diﬃculty here is that the algorithm must b e polynomial time
in the logarithm of the integer it is to factor, although it is permitted t o be merely sub-exponential in the
logarithm of the smoothness bound. That such an algorithm exists is by no means guaranteed.
Typically, the algorithm used here will be the Elliptic Curve Method, due to Lenstra [32]. For technical
reasons, we instead use the somewhat more complex Hyperelliptic Cu rve Method, which works on the
Jacobian of a hyperelliptic curve in place of an elliptic curve.
