and obtains, with probability at least \, all prime factors p of n with p ^ v.
The hyperelliptic curve method is of purely theoretical interest; the following
comparisons with other methods are on a theoretical basis only.
The deterministic algorithm of Pollard (1974) and Strassen (1977), also described
in Pomerance (1982), was heretofore the best algorithm known for finding all prime
